./.lattice/story/actives/B-9812/review-runs.json:15:      "assembledPrompt": "## Runtime Contract\n\nLifecycle: INIT -> INIT_CHECK -> PLAN -> DEV -> REVIEW -> TEST -> DONE.\nOnly the Story owner/implementer writes implementation; independent reviewers write signed findings or passes.\nStory and fixture facts use Lattice CLI paths; gate evidence is structured and fail-closed.\nNever fabricate host, human, provider, receipt, or Authority evidence.\n\n## Role Contract\n\n{\"allowedCommandIds\":[\"review_run_start\",\"finding_add\",\"review_pass_set\"],\"defaultDispatch\":true,\"forbiddenActionIds\":[\"fabricate-authority\",\"write-outside-role-boundary\"],\"renderDigest\":\"aa959585d8566f2974f4de6b636b92ec63a1d433eaebe7416341b12bf7e38f43\",\"requiredCheckIds\":[\"scope-and-authority-check\"],\"requiredInputIds\":[\"dispatch-target\",\"project-runtime-guide\"],\"requiredOutputIds\":[\"review-finding-or-pass\"],\"responsibility\":\"Review concept deletion and residual references.\",\"roleId\":\"lattice-review-concept\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.role-contract.v1\",\"semanticDigest\":\"197d76c8d93d85f4ec8cc45b581be70fd8526b4f971f5eeaaad23ca1b04f0ff2\",\"status\":\"active\",\"stopConditionCodes\":[\"missing-required-input\",\"authority-boundary\"]}\n\n## Task Context\n\n{\"checklist\":[{\"context\":\"Produce machine-readable timing, process-launch, membership, assertion, mutation, and failure baselines for the frozen current canonical inventory (45 members on the B-9812 base). Bidirectional completeness must incorporate any required member merged before final verification. Measure only in clean temporary clones after same-material builds.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[\"docs/dev/full-suite-performance.md\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/full-suite-baseline.ts\"],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/full-suite-baseline-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-001\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/done-full-test-gate-execution-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/test-runner-consolidation-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/testing-infra.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Establish a reproducible full-suite performance and coverage baseline\",\"userSees\":\"The terminal prints a machine-readable baseline naming every canonical member, its status and duration, and confirms the frozen inventory is complete with no duplicates or skips.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Mutate the baseline inventory by deleting one member, duplicating one member, and deleting one assertion or mutation signature in separate trials; the equivalence checker fails each trial with the exact missing or duplicate identity; WHY: a faster but smaller suite must be mechanically rejected.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Attempt to benchmark with mismatched source and dist material or with outputs written inside the project worktree; the collector refuses or reports a binding violation and leaves tracked files untouched; WHY: stale artifacts and benchmark pollution could create false performance evidence.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Measure from a temporary clone whose absolute path contains spaces and after clearing generated dist before the required same-material build; the collector attributes every member in the frozen current canonical inventory (45 on the B-9812 base, plus any later-merged required canonical members discovered by the bidirectional completeness contract) exactly once and binds results to the rebuilt HEAD/material hash; WHY: path quoting, stale-build assumptions, and later inventory growth must not corrupt or shrink the oracle.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Force one baseline member to exit nonzero after emitting partial output; the report preserves its timing and failure status, marks the overall run failed, and does not misclassify later absent members as passing; WHY: failure outcomes are part of the comparison contract.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"From a clean temporary clone at the story material HEAD, build packages/main and run the current canonical root suite baseline; emit machine-readable per-member wall, user, system, exit status, process-launch count, assertion inventory, mutation inventory, and failure outcome for the frozen current canonical inventory (45 on the B-9812 base), with bidirectional completeness requiring every later-merged required canonical member to enter the inventory and forbidding omissions, including the measured 1688.9-second historical reference; WHY: optimization needs a reproducible oracle for both speed and retained coverage without freezing an obsolete member count.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Run the baseline collector twice against unchanged material and compare normalized membership, assertion, mutation, and outcome inventories; all semantic inventories match while timings may vary, and the source worktree remains unchanged; WHY: the baseline must be deterministic and non-polluting.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Extend the smoke manifest and runner with parallel-safe, exclusive Git common-dir, exclusive fixed port or path, shared runtime lock, and main-write lock classifications. Run tasks concurrently only when isolation is proven. Require unique temporary roots and reliable child cleanup on timeout or interruption. Mechanically serialize conflicting resources, and default unknown classifications to fail closed or serial execution.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/smoke-manifest.json\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/run-all-smokes.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/run-all-smokes-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-002\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/session-ownership-and-write-leases.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/test-runner-consolidation-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/testing-infra.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Define and enforce a resource-isolation contract for concurrent tests\",\"userSees\":\"The runner reports each test's resource class and lock wait, runs compatible tests concurrently, and rejects unsafe or unclassified concurrent work.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Mutate the scheduler to ignore one protected resource key; a collision sentinel that holds the resource while writing an ownership token detects overlap and fails the test; WHY: the isolation test must bite if locking is removed.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Spawn a grandchild that ignores the first termination signal and keeps a file or port open, then timeout its member; the scheduler escalates termination for the owned process tree, reports TIMEOUT, and a probe proves no descendant or resource survives; WHY: killing only the direct child leaks interference into later tests.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Make cleanup target resolution point outside the task-owned temporary root; cleanup is refused and the external sentinel remains intact; WHY: concurrent cleanup must be bounded and non-destructive.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Give two lexically different paths that resolve through symlink or realpath to the same Git common-dir or fixed path; the scheduler canonicalizes them to one resource key and serializes the tasks; WHY: textual path inequality must not bypass isolation.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Run an unclassified manifest member and a member with an unknown resource kind; execution fails closed or runs serially with an explicit diagnostic, never concurrently by default; WHY: incomplete classifications must not become unsafe optimism.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Use jobs=1, jobs greater than member count, and a queue containing both exclusive and parallel-safe tasks; all members execute once without deadlock or starvation and statuses match; WHY: boundary worker counts and mixed locks exercise scheduler progress.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"Schedule at least two manifest tasks declared parallel-safe with distinct temporary roots; execution intervals overlap, both pass, and the report names their acquired resources and unique roots; WHY: the contract must enable real concurrency rather than merely describe it.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Schedule pairs sharing each protected class in turn: Git common-dir, fixed port or path, shared runtime lock, and main-write lock; conflicting intervals never overlap while unrelated work continues, and lock-wait time is recorded; WHY: every declared shared resource must be mechanically serialized.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"On normal completion, timeout, and external interruption, verify all worker descendants are terminated and every task-owned temporary root is removed without touching another task root; WHY: safe concurrency includes process-tree and filesystem lifecycle ownership.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Preserve real dist and CLI black-box sentinels and all rollout diagnostics, mutation and restoration checks, reviewer lanes, and quorum assertions. Generate each cohort once, freeze it with a signed digest, and reuse it. Run independent cases concurrently in isolated temporary repositories. Reuse an in-process context or batch entry for matrix checks that do not need repeated process-boundary verification, with explicit equivalence checks against the real CLI path.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/proofstory-acceptance-rollout-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/proofstory-pre-review-check-smoke.ts\",\"scripts/run-proofstory-acceptance-rollout-cohort.mjs\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/proofstory-acceptance-rollout-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-003\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/proofstory-acceptance-topology-and-pre-review-gates-execution-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/test-runner-consolidation-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/testing-completeness.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Eliminate duplicate acceptance rollout cohorts and repeated CLI cold starts\",\"userSees\":\"The acceptance rollout summary shows one digest-bound cohort generation, retained CLI sentinels, and every rollout diagnostic and restoration assertion passing.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Mutate the implementation to invoke cohort generation twice or accept an unsigned or stale cached cohort; a generation-count or digest-binding assertion fails; WHY: the principal duplicate-work regression must be directly killed.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Introduce a divergence that is visible only through the real CLI wrapper, such as argument normalization or exit-code mapping, while leaving the in-process handler unchanged; the CLI equivalence sentinel fails; WHY: replacing all black-box checks with handlers would hide entrypoint regressions.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Force two cases to share a repository or temporary path and write distinct ownership sentinels; the isolation guard rejects scheduling or the collision test fails before results can pass; WHY: concurrent cohort speedup must not rely on accidental non-overlap.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Tamper with one byte of the frozen cohort or change its bound material hash before reuse; digest verification rejects the artifact before any acceptance claim is made; WHY: reuse is safe only when identity and integrity are enforced.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Cause one concurrent cohort case to fail midway after mutation but before restoration; that case reports failure, its repository is restored or quarantined, sibling repositories remain unchanged, and the overall rollout fails; WHY: case isolation must survive partial execution.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Run with jobs=1 and with the supported parallel worker count; cohort membership, diagnostics, mutations, restorations, reviewer lanes, quorum outcomes, and digest are equivalent independent of completion order; WHY: concurrency must not alter semantics.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:edge:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"Run the optimized acceptance rollout and prove each logical cohort is generated exactly once, frozen with a content digest, and reused by all consumers; the complete prior diagnostics, mutation/restoration outcomes, reviewer-lane results, and quorum assertions equal the pinned baseline inventory; WHY: removing duplicate generation must not remove acceptance coverage.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Execute independent cohort cases concurrently in isolated temporary repositories and retain the required real dist and CLI black-box sentinel cases; every case passes once and the output records both batch/in-process and real-CLI paths; WHY: speedup must preserve process-boundary coverage where it matters.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"For every matrix check moved in-process or into a batch entry, run an equivalence sample through the real CLI and compare normalized exit class, diagnostic codes, and evidence artifacts; mismatches are zero; WHY: handler reuse must remain behaviorally equivalent to the production entrypoint.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:happy:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Safely shard independent scenarios and use deterministic seeds or schedules for mixed reviewer writers, ABA, cutoff, and restoration cases. Do not claim equivalence merely by reducing the twenty-iteration loop. If redundant burn-in moves to a stress layer, retain deterministic canonical cases that kill the same mutations and provide an old-versus-new assertion and failure-matrix comparison.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/proofstory-intent-hardening-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/review-incremental-context-smoke.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/proofstory-intent-hardening-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/review-incremental-context-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-004\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/review-run-binding-race.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/test-runner-consolidation-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/testing-completeness.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Reduce incremental-context and intent-hardening long tails without losing race coverage\",\"userSees\":\"The canonical suite reports deterministic incremental-context and intent-hardening coverage separately from optional burn-in, with the same injected mutations detected.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Reduce canonical schedules or iterations without supplying an equivalent mutation-kill mapping; the old-versus-new inventory comparison fails on the missing assertion or mutation class; WHY: raw speed cannot authorize silent race-coverage shrinkage.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Remove seed recording or introduce order-dependent shared state between shards; repeat/replay comparison detects nondeterminism or cross-shard contamination and fails; WHY: parallel tests must not exchange hidden state.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Mutate ABA, cutoff, or restoration guards one at a time; at least one retained deterministic canonical case fails for every mutation previously killed by the twenty-iteration suite; WHY: the reduced long tail must still bite the actual race protections.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Replay each failing randomized or scheduled scenario from its recorded seed and schedule under jobs=1; it reaches the same failure class and identifies the responsible lane or mutation; WHY: race failures must be diagnosable rather than flaky.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Exercise ABA transitions at the cutoff boundary and restoration immediately before and after the binding read; stale evidence is rejected and valid restored state is accepted exactly as in the baseline matrix; WHY: off-by-one timing is the core concurrency boundary.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Run a shard that times out beside successful shards; successful results remain attributable, the full command fails, and no state from the timed-out shard appears in another shard; WHY: partial shard completion must not contaminate evidence.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:edge:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"Run the deterministic canonical incremental-context schedules for mixed reviewer writers, ABA, cutoff, restoration, and intent-hardening mutations; every pinned assertion and failure-matrix cell from the old suite is present and produces the same outcome; WHY: shorter execution must preserve race and mutation coverage, not just lower iteration count.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Shard only scenarios declared independent and run them concurrently with deterministic seed or schedule recorded in the report; jobs=1 and parallel runs have identical normalized member, assertion, mutation, and failure outcomes; WHY: concurrency must be reproducible and semantically neutral.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"If redundant burn-in iterations move to a stress command, prove canonical root npm test still runs deterministic representatives that kill every previously covered mutation class and prove the stress command retains the full twenty-iteration campaign; WHY: classification may move probabilistic repetition but not coverage.\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:happy:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Replace the current 45-command serial chain with a resource-aware runner over the frozen current canonical inventory, with bidirectional checks that automatically expose omissions, duplicates, skips, and later required-member drift. Preserve focused test entries and make first FAIL/TIMEOUT terminal.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/full-suite-manifest.ts\"],\"modify\":[\"lattice.config.json\",\"package.json\",\"packages/main/smoke-manifest.json\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/run-all-smokes.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/run-all-smokes-smoke.ts\",\"scripts/verify-full-suite-membership.mjs\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-005\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/done-full-test-gate-execution-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/test-runner-consolidation-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/testing-infra.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Route canonical root npm test through the safe scheduler with complete membership\",\"userSees\":\"Running npm test executes the complete manifest through the safe scheduler, prints a critical-path summary, and exits nonzero on the first observed failed or timed-out member without retry masking.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Delete, duplicate, rename, or mark skipped one manifest member in separate mutations, including a required member merged after the B-9812 base; the bidirectional completeness contract fails before or during execution with the exact inventory discrepancy; WHY: omissions and duplicates are the easiest way to manufacture a faster suite, and later-required members must not fall outside a frozen snapshot.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Add a retry path that reruns an initial FAIL or TIMEOUT serially and returns only the later pass; a terminal-first-outcome test proves root remains failed and retains both observations without status laundering; WHY: retry must never mask the first authoritative failure.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Mutate result aggregation so a worker rejection, signal exit, or missing terminal record is treated as success; fail-closed aggregation tests make root npm test exit nonzero; WHY: scheduler plumbing failures must not become green builds.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Run with an empty filtered selection, an unknown member request, jobs=1, and jobs larger than the suite; invalid or empty selections fail explicitly where appropriate, and valid worker boundaries execute each selected member once; WHY: scheduler argument boundaries must not create silent success.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Queue a long exclusive member between many short parallel-safe members; the lock-aware scheduler eventually runs it without deadlock or starvation and records its wait; WHY: safety must not sacrifice progress.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Interrupt canonical npm test while members are active; root exits nonzero after bounded process-tree cleanup and emits a terminal interrupted status for started members rather than fabricated PASS or SKIP results; WHY: operator cancellation must preserve truthful terminal state.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:edge:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"Run canonical root npm test through the resource-aware scheduler and compare its manifest bidirectionally with the frozen current canonical inventory (45 on the B-9812 base) plus every later-merged required canonical member; every identity appears exactly once, no required later member can be omitted, no unexpected skip occurs, and all focused diagnostic entrypoints remain callable; WHY: replacing the shell chain must retain complete suite membership while allowing the authoritative inventory to grow.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Run the canonical manifest with jobs=1 and with safe parallelism; normalized member status, exit class, critical evidence, assertion inventory, and mutation inventory are equivalent, while the parallel report demonstrates overlap only for non-conflicting resources; WHY: scheduling must change time but not verdicts.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Make one member fail with a unique diagnostic; root npm test exits nonzero, reports the original first failure and member logs, and does not convert the result to pass through retry; WHY: the canonical command must remain trustworthy and debuggable.\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:happy:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"After a same-material build in a clean temporary clone, run canonical root npm test three consecutive times with every run below 300000 milliseconds and every member in the completeness-checked full set passing. Record per-member timing, critical path, worker utilization, and resource-lock wait. Establish jobs=1 result equivalence and use mutations that introduce shared-path conflicts, timeout, child leakage, and test failure to prove resource locking, cleanup, and fail-closed behavior. DONE-required receipts must still accurately record canonical root npm test.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[\"scripts/verify-full-suite-performance.mjs\"],\"modify\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/done-full-test-gate-execution-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/test-runner-consolidation-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/testing-infra.md\"],\"test\":[\"scripts/verify-full-suite-performance.mjs\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-006\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/done-full-test-gate-execution-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/testing-completeness.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/testing-infra.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Prove three consecutive sub-five-minute runs and concurrency safety\",\"userSees\":\"A clean-clone benchmark report shows three consecutive complete npm test runs below 300000 ms, jobs=1 equivalence, zero leaked children, and every safety mutation detected.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Inject, in separate trials, a shared-path collision, a fixed-port collision, a timeout with a surviving grandchild attempt, and an ordinary member failure; locking prevents unsafe overlap, cleanup leaves no descendant or resource, and every timeout or failure makes root npm test fail terminally; WHY: concurrency safety must be proven by failures that bite.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Tamper with timing output, drop a slow member, forge a PASS without a terminal record, or reuse evidence from another material hash; reconciliation, completeness, terminal-state, or freshness checks reject every trial; WHY: the sub-five-minute claim must resist evidence fabrication and suite shrinkage.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Mutate resource classification or lock acquisition so two known-conflicting sentinel members overlap; ownership-token assertions fail and no DONE-required PASS receipt is emitted; WHY: lifecycle evidence must be impossible when concurrency isolation regresses.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Execute the three-run proof with cold filesystem state for the first run and ordinary warm state thereafter without sharing task-owned temporary repositories between runs; every run remains below the limit and semantically equivalent; WHY: the threshold must not depend on a hidden dirty fixture.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Set available workers to one less and one more than the recommended default while preserving safe resource limits; runs either complete correctly or refuse unsupported capacity explicitly, with no oversubscription-induced false pass; WHY: the scheduler must handle realistic host variability safely.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Approach the 300000-millisecond boundary using a controlled slow member; elapsed time is measured by a monotonic clock, a run at or above the limit fails the performance assertion, and report serialization time cannot hide the breach; WHY: the acceptance threshold needs exact boundary semantics.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:edge:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"In a clean temporary clone bound to the implementation HEAD, perform the required same-material packages/main build and run canonical root npm test three consecutive times; each run executes the completeness-checked full set, all members pass, and each independently measured wall time is below 300000 milliseconds; WHY: the user-visible performance goal requires repeatable end-to-end proof rather than one warm outlier.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"For all three runs persist machine-readable per-member timing, critical path, worker utilization, resource-lock wait, process-launch counts, material identity, and terminal outcomes; totals reconcile with the root result and expose the bottleneck; WHY: the performance claim must be auditable and regression-ready.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Run the same material with jobs=1 and compare full membership, assertions, mutations, statuses, and critical evidence to the parallel runs; all semantic fields match even though jobs=1 need not meet the five-minute target; WHY: concurrency safety requires a serial oracle.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:happy:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Generate DONE-required validation evidence through the canonical root npm test path and verify the receipt names the exact command, HEAD/material/story-files hashes, exit status, full-suite identity, and fresh timing; WHY: optimization must not weaken the lifecycle gate evidence.\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:happy:3\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}}],\"description\":\"An isolated measurement at commit 58c7cdc showed that root npm test passed all 46 members on the measured B-cdf6 descendant but took 1688.9 seconds. The authoritative B-9812 base has a frozen current canonical inventory of 45 members; the descendant-only audit-scan-bin-token member is not silently imported, while bidirectional completeness must include any required member merged before final verification. proofstory-acceptance-rollout, review-incremental-context-smoke, and proofstory-intent-hardening-smoke consumed 79.9 percent of the measured total. One acceptance cohort case took 26.42 seconds, with about 95.2 percent spent in 26 fresh-process Lattice CLI invocations while Git and build together took less than 0.5 seconds. Implement safe concurrency and eliminate redundant initialization so canonical root npm test completes in less than 300 seconds on each of three consecutive runs from a reproducible clean temporary clone after a same-material packages/main build. Preserve the complete frozen test membership, deterministic assertions, mutation bites, black-box dist and CLI boundaries, and DONE-required evidence semantics. The target must not be met by deleting tests, silently reducing coverage, moving required members out of the canonical full suite, concurrently writing an unisolated repository, or converting an initial FAIL or TIMEOUT into PASS through serial retry.\",\"headHash\":\"e60bfdece8125834e42863b8188b5a7af886de3f\",\"materialHash\":\"40111627f13b42e3ad525d8d3058953de8a8672825cd3f3660351dfb2c9cecc9\",\"phase\":\"REVIEW\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.full-task-context.v1\",\"scope\":{\"allowedCreate\":[\"docs/dev/full-suite-performance.md\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/full-suite-*.ts\",\"scripts/verify-full-suite-*.mjs\"],\"allowedModify\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/done-full-test-gate-execution-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/proofstory-acceptance-topology-and-pre-review-gates-execution-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/role-prompt-modularization-and-budget-execution-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/test-runner-consolidation-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/testing-infra.md\",\"lattice.config.json\",\"package.json\",\"packages/main/package.json\",\"packages/main/smoke-manifest.json\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/proofstory-acceptance-rollout-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/proofstory-intent-hardening-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/proofstory-pre-review-check-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/review-incremental-context-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/run-all-smokes-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/run-all-smokes.ts\",\"scripts/run-proofstory-acceptance-rollout-cohort.mjs\"],\"allowedTest\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/*smoke.ts\",\"scripts/verify-*.mjs\"],\"explicitExcludes\":[\".githooks/**\",\".github/**\",\"packages/main/src/core/**\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/**\",\"packages/main/src/mcp/**\"],\"fileRules\":[],\"mode\":\"enforce\",\"pathCanonicalizationMode\":\"enforce\",\"pathCanonicalizerVersion\":\"repo-relative-v1\",\"protectedAnchors\":[],\"protectedFiles\":[\"packages/main/src/core/done-required-validation.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/process-fact-registry.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/runtime-fact-registry.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/phase-gates.ts\"]},\"scopeContractDigest\":\"08d83579b73594f67f6c4cd92d4f2b1e7612466f8b533a781b2eec794b3273ca\",\"storyFilesHash\":\"58996eb5f1c522784ce914873d085158f1ef5bf9581bdf3691e9f734296ab83e\",\"storyId\":\"B-9812\",\"title\":\"Run the complete root test suite safely in parallel in under five minutes\"}\n\n## Known Execution Environment\n\n{\"architecture\":\"arm64\",\"cliVersion\":\"0.3.251\",\"nodeVersion\":\"v26.5.1\",\"platform\":\"darwin\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.known-execution-environment.v1\",\"source\":\"trusted-local-runtime\"}\n\n## Dispatch Prompt\n\nAs lattice-review-concept, review story B-9812 using the trusted context selected by review_run_start.\n\nWorking directory (subagent must cd here): /Users/qipan/work/repo/Prooforstop/.worktrees/B-9812\n\nExecution rhythm / liveness:\n- After starting, first output `DISPATCH_START:lattice-review-concept/story` so the main agent knows the process has started.\n- If there is no output for 4 minutes, the main agent should ask about status once; if there is still no result after 10 minutes/600s, consider it stalled and feel free to restart this reviewer/worker.\n- If this is a retry, please explain the previous stalled state in the final reply, to avoid mistaking network/startup failures for review conclusions.\n\nRole boundary:\n- Review only; do not change code, tests, checklist status, or story metadata.\n- This is a story-level dispatch: review every checklist item and the integrated change, not one selected item.\n\nRequired reading:\n1. .lattice/story/actives/B-9812/background.md\n2. .lattice/story/actives/B-9812/plan.md\n3. .lattice/story/actives/B-9812/checklist.json\n- Read the files and relatedDocs named by every checklist item, bounded by the current candidate-spec artifact.\n\nCurrent phase: REVIEW. Review lane: lattice-review-concept.\nConclusion record (must choose one):\n- Start the reviewer run: lattice review_run_start '{\"storyId\":\"B-9812\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\"}' and copy the returned reviewRunId.\n- Has issues: lattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"B-9812\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId>\",\"desc\":\"<file:line WHY + severity>\",\"severity\":\"high|medium|low\",\"category\":\"missing|edge|adversarial|happy\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\"}'\n- No blocker: call review_pass_set with the returned reviewRunId and a truthful readManifest covering the story-level review.\n\n## Role Prompt\n\n---\nname: lattice-review-concept\ndescription: REVIEW review: concept deletion completeness (grep scan for residuals)\nmodel: sonnet\ntools: Grep, Glob, Bash\n---\n<!-- proofbound:modular-role-body:v1 -->\n## Closing Self-Check (Mandatory after completing first-pass check)\n\nAfter completing all checks below, additionally ask yourself: **Does this diff contain any \"promised but undelivered\" parts?** Any `lattice <cmd>` examples newly added to CLAUDE.md / README, handler schema fields, ENV variables, or behavior paragraphs — all must be cross-checked against the code to verify corresponding implementations exist. If \"promised but undelivered\" is found → **critical finding** (category=`missing`, prefix desc with `doc-promise-undelivered:`).\n\n## 0. Project Context\nThe Lattice framework conventions above (auto-injected by build) define the system architecture and concepts.\n\nYou only do one thing: check whether this change deletes or replaces a concept, and if so, grep the entire repository to confirm zero residue.\n\n## Process\n\n1. `git diff main...HEAD --stat` to see which files changed\n2. `git diff main...HEAD` to see specific changes, and identify **concept words that have been deleted/replaced en masse** (e.g., testIntent was deleted, alpha was replaced with beta)\n3. For each identified concept word, grep the entire repository (excluding node_modules / dist / .git):\n   ```bash\n   grep -rn 'concept-word' . --include='*.ts' --include='*.md' --include='*.json' | grep -v node_modules | grep -v dist | grep -v '.git/' | grep -v '@deprecated'\n   ```\n4. grep result > 0 → file a finding:\n   ```bash\n   lattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"desc\":\"concept-cleanup: concept X deletion incomplete: Y file still has N references\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"category\":\"missing\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\"}'\n   ```\n5. No concept deletion/replacement → forbidden to use `finding_add` to record pass-only; call `lattice review_pass_set '{\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\",\"note\":\"No concept deletion/replacement this round; concept residue check completed, no blocker.\"}'`\n\n## Input Constraints (fresh-context hygiene)\n\nYour input contains only the following, and does NOT include the main agent's full conversation history:\n\n- `git diff main...HEAD` (code changes)\n- checklist item (title / context / userSees)\n- corresponding section in plan.md (if any)\n- necessary understanding / decision summaries (if any)\n\n**Forbidden**:\n- Do not assume you know the main agent's intent or context — only infer from the inputs above\n- Do not be led astray by narrative — only look at deliverables (code diff + checklist declarations)\n- If the inputs are insufficient to make a judgment, file a medium finding describing what information is missing\n\n## Rules\n\n- Only grep, do not modify code\n- **Every finding must be registered via `lattice finding_add`; describing it only in text is forbidden. An unregistered finding equals no discovery.**\n- finding_add must include the agent parameter, with the value being this reviewer's name (e.g., \"lattice-review-concept\"), to ensure correct finding attribution.\n- The first action of the current REVIEW round is `review_run_start`; if code or documentation continues to change during the review, the current run becomes stale and must go back to DEV for a fix and re-submission, then DEV→REVIEW enters a new round — do not re-run it as a fix within the same REVIEW round.\n- After the review ends, confirm that all discovered issues have been registered via `lattice finding_add`, then output the number of registered findings as the final summary\n- When there are no findings, forbidden to use `finding_add` to pad a pass; must call `lattice review_pass_set` to record the scope this reviewer has checked and the reason for no blocker.\n- When the current REVIEW round begins, first call `lattice review_run_start {\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"agent\":\"<reviewer-name>\"}`; record the returned `reviewRunId`, and all `finding_add` / `review_pass_set` in this round must carry this field.\n- Example of pass record with no blocker: `lattice review_pass_set {\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"agent\":\"<reviewer-name>\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"note\":\"...\"}`.\n- Items marked with @deprecated do not count as residue\n- References in comments also count as residue (comments mislead future developers)\n- Items retained for backward compat (e.g., old phase enum values in types.ts) do not count, but must be confirmed to have a backward compat comment\n\nWave 4 concept boundary: verify the canonical verifier-owned chain `acceptance_topology_check` → `pre_review_check_read` → `acceptance_rollout_report_read` / `acceptance_rollout_check`; prompt prose is not evidence. Require a current signed PASS receipt and genuine full 3 rounds × 2 hosts (`codex-cli` + `claude-cli`), reject degraded 3x1, keep diagnostics/status invariant across observe/warn/enforce, and confirm rollback only changes `proofStory.acceptanceRolloutGateMode` while preserving history.\n",
./.lattice/story/actives/B-9812/review-runs.json:399:      "assembledPrompt": "## Runtime Contract\n\nLifecycle: INIT -> INIT_CHECK -> PLAN -> DEV -> REVIEW -> TEST -> DONE.\nOnly the Story owner/implementer writes implementation; independent reviewers write signed findings or passes.\nStory and fixture facts use Lattice CLI paths; gate evidence is structured and fail-closed.\nNever fabricate host, human, provider, receipt, or Authority evidence.\n\n## Role Contract\n\n{\"allowedCommandIds\":[\"review_run_start\",\"finding_add\",\"review_pass_set\"],\"defaultDispatch\":true,\"forbiddenActionIds\":[\"fabricate-authority\",\"write-outside-role-boundary\"],\"renderDigest\":\"aa959585d8566f2974f4de6b636b92ec63a1d433eaebe7416341b12bf7e38f43\",\"requiredCheckIds\":[\"scope-and-authority-check\"],\"requiredInputIds\":[\"dispatch-target\",\"project-runtime-guide\"],\"requiredOutputIds\":[\"review-finding-or-pass\"],\"responsibility\":\"Review concept deletion and residual references.\",\"roleId\":\"lattice-review-concept\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.role-contract.v1\",\"semanticDigest\":\"197d76c8d93d85f4ec8cc45b581be70fd8526b4f971f5eeaaad23ca1b04f0ff2\",\"status\":\"active\",\"stopConditionCodes\":[\"missing-required-input\",\"authority-boundary\"]}\n\n## Task Context\n\n{\"checklist\":[{\"context\":\"Produce machine-readable timing, process-launch, membership, assertion, mutation, and failure baselines for the frozen current canonical inventory (45 members on the B-9812 base). Bidirectional completeness must incorporate any required member merged before final verification. Measure only in clean temporary clones after same-material builds.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[\"docs/dev/full-suite-performance.md\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/full-suite-baseline.ts\"],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/full-suite-baseline-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-001\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/done-full-test-gate-execution-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/test-runner-consolidation-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/testing-infra.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Establish a reproducible full-suite performance and coverage baseline\",\"userSees\":\"The terminal prints a machine-readable baseline naming every canonical member, its status and duration, and confirms the frozen inventory is complete with no duplicates or skips.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Mutate the baseline inventory by deleting one member, duplicating one member, and deleting one assertion or mutation signature in separate trials; the equivalence checker fails each trial with the exact missing or duplicate identity; WHY: a faster but smaller suite must be mechanically rejected.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Attempt to benchmark with mismatched source and dist material or with outputs written inside the project worktree; the collector refuses or reports a binding violation and leaves tracked files untouched; WHY: stale artifacts and benchmark pollution could create false performance evidence.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Measure from a temporary clone whose absolute path contains spaces and after clearing generated dist before the required same-material build; the collector attributes every member in the frozen current canonical inventory (45 on the B-9812 base, plus any later-merged required canonical members discovered by the bidirectional completeness contract) exactly once and binds results to the rebuilt HEAD/material hash; WHY: path quoting, stale-build assumptions, and later inventory growth must not corrupt or shrink the oracle.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Force one baseline member to exit nonzero after emitting partial output; the report preserves its timing and failure status, marks the overall run failed, and does not misclassify later absent members as passing; WHY: failure outcomes are part of the comparison contract.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"From a clean temporary clone at the story material HEAD, build packages/main and run the current canonical root suite baseline; emit machine-readable per-member wall, user, system, exit status, process-launch count, assertion inventory, mutation inventory, and failure outcome for the frozen current canonical inventory (45 on the B-9812 base), with bidirectional completeness requiring every later-merged required canonical member to enter the inventory and forbidding omissions, including the measured 1688.9-second historical reference; WHY: optimization needs a reproducible oracle for both speed and retained coverage without freezing an obsolete member count.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Run the baseline collector twice against unchanged material and compare normalized membership, assertion, mutation, and outcome inventories; all semantic inventories match while timings may vary, and the source worktree remains unchanged; WHY: the baseline must be deterministic and non-polluting.\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Extend the smoke manifest and runner with parallel-safe, exclusive Git common-dir, exclusive fixed port or path, shared runtime lock, and main-write lock classifications. Run tasks concurrently only when isolation is proven. Require unique temporary roots and reliable child cleanup on timeout or interruption. Mechanically serialize conflicting resources, and default unknown classifications to fail closed or serial execution.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/smoke-manifest.json\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/run-all-smokes.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/run-all-smokes-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-002\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/session-ownership-and-write-leases.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/test-runner-consolidation-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/testing-infra.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Define and enforce a resource-isolation contract for concurrent tests\",\"userSees\":\"The runner reports each test's resource class and lock wait, runs compatible tests concurrently, and rejects unsafe or unclassified concurrent work.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Mutate the scheduler to ignore one protected resource key; a collision sentinel that holds the resource while writing an ownership token detects overlap and fails the test; WHY: the isolation test must bite if locking is removed.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Spawn a grandchild that ignores the first termination signal and keeps a file or port open, then timeout its member; the scheduler escalates termination for the owned process tree, reports TIMEOUT, and a probe proves no descendant or resource survives; WHY: killing only the direct child leaks interference into later tests.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Make cleanup target resolution point outside the task-owned temporary root; cleanup is refused and the external sentinel remains intact; WHY: concurrent cleanup must be bounded and non-destructive.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Give two lexically different paths that resolve through symlink or realpath to the same Git common-dir or fixed path; the scheduler canonicalizes them to one resource key and serializes the tasks; WHY: textual path inequality must not bypass isolation.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Run an unclassified manifest member and a member with an unknown resource kind; execution fails closed or runs serially with an explicit diagnostic, never concurrently by default; WHY: incomplete classifications must not become unsafe optimism.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Use jobs=1, jobs greater than member count, and a queue containing both exclusive and parallel-safe tasks; all members execute once without deadlock or starvation and statuses match; WHY: boundary worker counts and mixed locks exercise scheduler progress.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"Schedule at least two manifest tasks declared parallel-safe with distinct temporary roots; execution intervals overlap, both pass, and the report names their acquired resources and unique roots; WHY: the contract must enable real concurrency rather than merely describe it.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Schedule pairs sharing each protected class in turn: Git common-dir, fixed port or path, shared runtime lock, and main-write lock; conflicting intervals never overlap while unrelated work continues, and lock-wait time is recorded; WHY: every declared shared resource must be mechanically serialized.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"On normal completion, timeout, and external interruption, verify all worker descendants are terminated and every task-owned temporary root is removed without touching another task root; WHY: safe concurrency includes process-tree and filesystem lifecycle ownership.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Preserve real dist and CLI black-box sentinels and all rollout diagnostics, mutation and restoration checks, reviewer lanes, and quorum assertions. Generate each cohort once, freeze it with a signed digest, and reuse it. Run independent cases concurrently in isolated temporary repositories. Reuse an in-process context or batch entry for matrix checks that do not need repeated process-boundary verification, with explicit equivalence checks against the real CLI path.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/proofstory-acceptance-rollout-smoke.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/proofstory-pre-review-check-smoke.ts\",\"scripts/run-proofstory-acceptance-rollout-cohort.mjs\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/proofstory-acceptance-rollout-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-003\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"docs/requirements/decisions/proofstory-acceptance-topology-and-pre-review-gates-execution-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/test-runner-consolidation-plan.md\",\"docs/requirements/decisions/testing-completeness.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Eliminate duplicate acceptance rollout cohorts and repeated CLI cold starts\",\"userSees\":\"The acceptance rollout summary shows one digest-bound cohort generation, retained CLI sentinels, and every rollout diagnostic and restoration assertion passing.\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Mutate the implementation to invoke cohort generation twice or accept an unsigned or stale cached cohort; a generation-count or digest-binding assertion fails; WHY: the principal duplicate-work regression must be directly killed.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Introduce a divergence that is visible only through the real CLI wrapper, such as argument normalization or exit-code mapping, while leaving the in-process handler unchanged; the CLI equivalence sentinel fails; WHY: replacing all black-box checks with handlers would hide entrypoint regressions.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Force two cases to share a repository or temporary path and write distinct ownership sentinels; the isolation guard rejects scheduling or the collision test fails before results can pass; WHY: concurrent cohort speedup must not rely on accidental non-overlap.\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\